From ebe64d2595a2ccd1caebeb0ff15e00b97e63c527 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:06:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] List changes and presence go straight to the person's other
 computers, ahead of the registry room

A new chat, rename, archive, pin or status change on one of the person's
computers reached the others only through the edge's RegistryRoom, and
with the edge down not at all; who was online wasn't known either.

- PeerListOps over a proven road to devices with registry-peer-v1, never
  the relay; each beat calls every peer, so who's online holds with the
  edge down; a peer back is sent what it missed.
- Taken only from a device direct_peer admits, within a call budget, ops
  naming it and passing the room's rules; shown through a peer overlay
  with the registry's newest-wins merge, never pushed on, never moving the
  cursor; room rows supersede them; unconfirmed ones expire. A peer's word
  alone never says which device hosts a chat.
- An update to a row known only through a peer waits for the room's row.
- One table of merge vectors checks the overlay, the registry's merge and
  the edge's alike.
- docs/registry-sync.md, ARCHITECTURE.md.

Tests: peer_overlay's 23, peer_list's 3, peer_presence's 1,
peer_list_sync's 2, peer_list_offline's 9.
